============================================================================
(b) SAME for |R|, and the pair — is the signed count's poly-determined depth different?
============================================================================
 n=4: R: M=0  v2=inf    n=4: H: M=0  v2=inf   
 n=5: R: M=0  v2=inf    n=5: H: M=0  v2=inf   
 n=6: R: M=0  v2=inf    n=6: H: M=0  v2=inf   

============================================================================
(c) THE SPLIT: H = (formula part, poly-time) + M*(#P core).  Show the residual is genuinely free.
============================================================================
 n=6: M=0. Within a split poly-cell, H takes values differing by multiples of 0;
        the low inf bit(s) of H are the FORMULA part (Redei parity), the rest is the #P core.

============================================================================
(d) THE CRITICAL LENGTH (THM-1870 re-confirmed here): c_{n-1} spectral, c_n not
============================================================================
 n=4: c_3 spectral (constant on cospectral classes)? True
 n=4: c_4 spectral (constant on cospectral classes)? True <-- HAMILTONIAN LENGTH

 n=5: c_3 spectral (constant on cospectral classes)? True
 n=5: c_4 spectral (constant on cospectral classes)? True
 n=5: c_5 spectral (constant on cospectral classes)? True <-- HAMILTONIAN LENGTH

 n=6: c_3 spectral (constant on cospectral classes)? True
 n=6: c_4 spectral (constant on cospectral classes)? True
 n=6: c_5 spectral (constant on cospectral classes)? True
 n=6: c_6 spectral (constant on cospectral classes)? False <-- HAMILTONIAN LENGTH

DONE.
